# Logic Change Checklist

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Use this checklist for every correctness/completeness change that affects monitor runtime logic.

## Inputs and Contracts

- Identify the upstream contract being changed (sample line shape, `$` schema line, host token position, `st_name`, device id, event key).
- Document the canonical consumer source: **`HPCPerfStats/hpcperfstats/listend.py`** (read-only) per **`monitor-workspace-contract.mdc`**.
- Verify cross-layer consistency (monitor emit → listend host extraction → `archive_dir/<host>/current`).

## Invariants

- Define expected invariants before and after change (cadence, tier gating, cumulative vs gauge `E`, schema rotation on `$` messages).
- Verify no-data and collector-failure fallbacks remain deterministic.
- Verify config assumptions (`enable_slow_tier`, RabbitMQ exchange, trim rules).

## Failure Modes

- List at least one transient failure scenario (RabbitMQ disconnect, sysfs read failure, LIKWID/DCGM probe failure) and expected fallback.
- Confirm errors are logged with actionable context and do not silently corrupt emit state.
- Confirm retry and cooldown behavior is bounded per **`monitor-jitter-and-fidelity-priority.mdc`**.

## Regression Tests

- Add or update targeted unit/contract tests in `HPCPerfStats/monitor/tests/`.
- For emit/schema changes, include golden contract tests and negative assertions for retired keys.
- When consumer would break, attach **Consumer follow-up plan** per **`monitor-consumer-side-plan.mdc`** (do not edit consumer without user authorization).

## Validation Runbook

- Run smallest targeted `tests/test_*.c` first via `make check`.
- Run **`build_static_bundle.sh`** + **`make check`** for substantive C changes.
- Run **`cross_compile_test.sh`** when architecture/portability risk exists.
- Record what passed, what was skipped, and residual risks under **`test_runs/`**.

## Overlap

- **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`** — general plan-before-code and post-implementation self-review; use this checklist when runtime logic changes.
- Complements **`traceback-fix-discipline.mdc`**, **`monitor-collect-tier-gating.mdc`**, and **`monitor-c-testing-standards.mdc`**.
